accessWidener v2 official

# Kept in step with META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg, which is what `common` compiles against; this is Fabric's half.

# A biome's rainfall, which the server's sketch tints grass and leaves by (`BiomeTints`).
accessible class net/minecraft/world/level/biome/Biome$ClimateSettings
accessible field net/minecraft/world/level/biome/Biome climateSettings Lnet/minecraft/world/level/biome/Biome$ClimateSettings;

# Vanilla's table of special item models, which the recorded image's own picture is drawn through on Fabric
# (`RecordedImageRenderer`). Fabric API's transitive wideners open it, and this project leaves those to the loader.
accessible field net/minecraft/client/renderer/special/SpecialModelRenderers ID_MAPPER Lnet/minecraft/util/ExtraCodecs$LateBoundIdMapper;

# Vanilla's table of container screens, which the set-down recorder's screen joins on Fabric (`ImagingFabricClient`);
# NeoForge registers through an event. Fabric API's transitive wideners open it, and this project leaves those to the
# loader.
accessible method net/minecraft/client/gui/screens/MenuScreens register (Lnet/minecraft/world/inventory/MenuType;Lnet/minecraft/client/gui/screens/MenuScreens$ScreenConstructor;)V
accessible class net/minecraft/client/gui/screens/MenuScreens$ScreenConstructor

# So the set-down recorder's MenuType can be built in `common`, as Ages and the Art widens it for its own; its widener is
# the loader's to apply, and this project compiles without it.
accessible method net/minecraft/world/inventory/MenuType <init> (Lnet/minecraft/world/inventory/MenuType$MenuSupplier;Lnet/minecraft/world/flag/FeatureFlagSet;)V
